> [!IMPORTANT]
> Flashing a custom kernel carries risk of instability, bootloops, or other issues.
> You are flashing at your own risk — the maintainer is not responsible for any damage to your device.

---

## About

Tropsi X is an independent kernel build for the OnePlus kona platform, based on [ppajda's XTD kernel](https://github.com/ppajda). Built with a full LLVM toolchain and tuned for a snappier, more efficient daily-driver experience.

**Branch:** `sm8250_t_13.1_op8`

---

## Features

- [x] **Toolchain**
  - [x] Neutron Clang 19.0.0 + Neutron LLD
  - [x] Full LLVM build (Clang + LLD, no GCC)
- [x] **Root**
  - [x] KernelSU support baked in
- [x] **Performance**
  - [x] Zen I/O scheduler
  - [x] ZRAM swap tuned to 4GB with LZ4 compression
  - [x] Input boost frequency and duration tuning
- [x] **Networking**
  - [x] Westwood TCP congestion control

---

## Supported Devices

| Device | Codename | Models |
|---|---|---|
| OnePlus 8 | `instantnoodle` | IN2010 / IN2011 / IN2013 / IN2015 / IN2017 / IN2019 |
| OnePlus 8 Pro | `instantnoodlep` | IN2020 / IN2021 / IN2023 / IN2025 |
| OnePlus 8T | `kebab` | KB2000 / KB2001 / KB2003 / KB2005 |
| OnePlus 9R | `lemonades` | LE2100 / LE2101 |

---

## Installation

1. Grab the latest build from [Releases](https://github.com/TropsPk/Tropsi_X_Kernel/releases).
2. Flash via custom recovery (AnyKernel3 zip) or Fastboot.
3. Reboot and enjoy.

---

## Build from Source

```bash
git clone https://github.com/TropsPk/Tropsi_X_Kernel.git -b sm8250_t_13.1_op8
cd Tropsi_X_Kernel

make O=out ARCH=arm64 <your_defconfig>
make O=out ARCH=arm64 -j$(nproc --all)
```

